        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\n\n`:!` is intentionally a \"pipe\", not special-cased for TUI. Documented:\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/82c5891a2774513b3e0abcda0832ba85368cb607/runtime/doc/vim_diff.txt#L484-L485\n\n\n> I can do it in vim and not in nvim, so I reported it as a bug.\n\n`:te` doesn't work in Vim, it must be spelled `:term`. Did you report that bug there?\n\n> Like vim, a new instance starts using the window and on exit returns back to the previous instance.\n\nWe do have tentative plans to restore `:shell` or something like that.\n\nMeanwhile, this is a duplicate of:\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/1496\n\n\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-17T18:11:41Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41957#issuecomment-5719100030",
